  "body": "Cold-cluster native apps can arrive before their declared policy window. Make the apps Flux Kustomization depend on every actual composed route: policy 5, 6, 7 and machinery. The regression expands the repository's ResourceSet and rejects missing routes, unknown dependencies and cycles.\n\nThe moved selfcheck previously corrupted retained forward-intel v1 while the current emitter publishes v2. Derive the current feed from its single literal `VERSION`, test stale current bytes, and prove retained major history does not trigger the current clock. Re-render the comparison fingerprint with the authentic pinned tools.\n\nValidation: 28 enabled public tests passed with the real estate and no skips; authenticated tools5 compose, byte replay and signed-target reach passed; the exact-head normal gate measured `none` with no policy additions or retirements; normal SSH signature and post-commit byte verification passed. The moved check has four offline passes and retains its live `SKIP` (exit 3).\n\nFlux dependency readiness establishes delivery ordering. Actual webhook mutation and served-workload cage stamps still require the scheduled primary observations. Apps A, composition B, primary inventory, native claims, engine 1.18.2 and gated cloud settings are preserved.\n\n<!-- cs-29:adopter-gate:start -->\n### adopter gate: platform's evidence, composed for driftwood\n\n**Composed bump: `none`** (publisher declared: `none`)\n\n- no change to the supported policy-version window\n<!-- cs-29:adopter-gate:end -->\n",
